### Health of the mock credit bureau: direct call (same request the REST Connector sends)
POST http://localhost:8090/credit-bureau/api/v1/assessments
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: LA-1001

< ./credit-assessment.request.json

### Simulated HTTP 500 (applicant SYN-9500)
POST http://localhost:8090/credit-bureau/api/v1/assessments
Content-Type: application/json

{"applicationId": "LA-1007", "applicantId": "SYN-9500", "monthlyIncome": 150000, "existingMonthlyEmi": 20000, "loanAmount": 900000}

### Start a loan application through the lab app
POST http://localhost:8091/api/process-instances
Content-Type: application/json

< ./start-instance.request.json

### Start a loan application directly through the Camunda 8 REST API (v2)
POST http://localhost:8080/v2/process-instances
Content-Type: application/json

< ./camunda-rest-create-instance.request.json

### Start a predefined scenario
POST http://localhost:8091/api/scenarios/03-manual-review/start

### Live results table
GET http://localhost:8091/api/scenarios/results.md

### Fault injection: every credit call fails / is slow / back to normal
PUT http://localhost:8090/admin/faults/credit?mode=DOWN
###
PUT http://localhost:8090/admin/faults/credit?mode=SLOW
###
PUT http://localhost:8090/admin/faults/credit?mode=UP
